{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"b44t1vn42","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GnpeyoW3dhgTHRxojVNjmo","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run3-repo/659947dd-e124-47b6-883c-21c12f5465d1/tasks/b44t1vn42.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_4\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of `local_representativeness` (Kahneman & Tversky's local representativeness: a sequence looks random to the extent it is locally balanced at several window scales and irregular, i.e. somewhat over-alternating but not periodic). The one change: people share this representativeness criterion but differ in how consistently they apply it, so each participant has their own decision sensitivity (drawn from a population distribution) rather than one shared sensitivity — addressing the critique that participants differ in agreement with the majority far more than a single pooled sensitivity allows.\nEOF\necho local_representativeness_person_sensitivity > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'PY'\nD=\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/\"\nsrc=open(D+\"models/local_representativeness.py\").read()\nhead, tail = src.split(\"with pm.Model() as model:\",1)\nbody, helpers = tail.split(\"# ─────\",1)\nhelpers = \"# ─────\"+helpers\ndoc = '''\"\"\"Refinement of `local_representativeness` with person-specific sensitivity.\n\nKahneman & Tversky local representativeness: a sequence looks random to the\nextent it is locally balanced (multi-scale window imbalance) and irregular\n(near an over-alternating prototype, not periodic). The single change from the\nincumbent: each participant applies this shared criterion with their own\ndecision sensitivity (log-normal population, non-centred), instead of one\npooled sensitivity.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pymc as pm\nimport pytensor.tensor as pt\n\nN_PERSON_SLOTS = 400\n\nwith pm.Model() as model:\n    participant_id = pm.Data(\"participant_id\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"int64\"))\n'''\nbody = body.replace('''    beta = pm.Uniform(\"beta\", lower=0.2, upper=12.0)\n''','''    beta = pm.Uniform(\"beta\", lower=0.2, upper=12.0)\n    sigma_beta = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_beta\", sigma=0.7)\n    z_beta = pm.Normal(\"z_beta\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=N_PERSON_SLOTS)\n    beta_person = beta * pt.exp(sigma_beta * z_beta - 0.5 * sigma_beta**2)\n''').replace(\"sigmoid(beta * (score_a\",\"sigmoid(beta_person[participant_id] * (score_a\")\nassert \"beta_person[participant_id]\" in body\nopen(D+\"iter_0/candidate_4/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(doc+body+helpers)\nPY\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses $D/../../responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"afb2b21b-987a-4c7c-9cfb-e12a04126e26","session_id":"659947dd-e124-47b6-883c-21c12f5465d1"}
